@copilot Update PR #21402 directly on its verified branch `copilot/javaagent-unit-test-rollout-batch-1` in `open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation`. Keep the branch GitHub Copilot cloud agent assigned. Do not rename it, replace it, or create another PR. If GitHub itself assigns a follow-up branch, keep it.

Address Copilot review 6007299136 and preserve the original scope: restore the original `check { dependsOn(testing.suites) }` wiring in the eight modules whose checks now enumerate other suites. Under `instrumentation/`, these are `couchbase/couchbase-3.2`, `influxdb-2.4`, `jedis/jedis-2.0`, `jms/jms-1.1`, `lettuce/lettuce-5.0`, `spring/spring-ai-1.0`, `spring/spring-jms/spring-jms-2.0`, and `spring/spring-rabbit-1.1`. All their registered suites belonged in `check` before the migration, and `.github/instructions/instrumentation-gradle.instructions.md` prefers collection wiring in that case. Keep the 24 `unitTests()` conversions and leave the other 16 modules alone. Preserve all existing suite-local dependencies, test versions, modes and gates. No production changes.

Apply the narrow Spotless tasks first, then compare `check` task graphs for these modules in baseline and latest-dependency modes where feasible. Report any concrete limitations in your run. Do not reply to or resolve review threads; the coordinator handles the review after verifying the fix.
